## Audit actor (EPIC F — P1-T-117)

All platform mutators pass **`ctx.actorId`** (ops phone from auth) into saga / lifecycle services. `appendPlatformAuditEvent` stores non-null `actorId` on `TENANT_CREATED`, `TENANT_UPDATED`, and invite actions — never anonymous platform audit rows.

`POST /platform/v1/tenants` uses the authenticated phone, not a hard-coded stub.

### Owner invite actor id (EPIC H fix)

`operator_pending_invites.invited_by_user_id` is a **UUID column** (tenant membership schema). Platform ops auth exposes **`actorId` as the ops phone** for audit rows only.

Provisioning and owner-invite resend therefore map platform actions to a fixed sentinel:

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| `appendPlatformAuditEvent.actorId` | authenticated ops phone |
| `operatorPendingInvite.invitedByUserId` | `00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000201` (`PLATFORM_PROVISION_INVITE_ACTOR_USER_ID`) |

Invite accept still keys off `inviteToken` + invitee phone match; the sentinel id is not validated as a tenant user.

## Site health timeout (EPIC F — P1-T-118)

`checkTenantSitesHealth` HEAD probes use **`AbortSignal.timeout(5000)`** per URL. Slow or unreachable hosts return `{ ok: false, status: null }` instead of hanging the request thread.

## Platform ops team & RBAC (EPIC G)

### PlatformOpsUser schema

Prisma model `platform_ops_users`:

| Column | Notes |
|--------|-------|
| `phone` | unique E.164-ish string |
| `role` | `owner` \| `admin` \| `support` |

No password column — auth remains header + OTP session stub in P1.

### Auth resolution

`assertPlatformOpsAuth` (async):

1. Require `Authorization` + `X-Platform-Ops-Phone`.
2. If phone exists in **`platform_ops_users`** → `{ actorId: phone, roles: [dbRole] }` (**DB overrides env default**).
3. Else if `PLATFORM_OPS_PHONES` CSV is non-empty and phone not listed → **403**.
4. Else → legacy env path `{ roles: ["owner"] }`.

Write guard: `assertPlatformOpsWriteRole` — `owner` and `admin` only; `support` read-only.

Owner-only guard: `assertPlatformOpsOwnerRole` — team membership mutations.

### Seed script

`apps/api/scripts/seed-platform-ops.ts` — idempotent upsert from **`PLATFORM_OPS_SEED`** CSV (`phone:role` pairs, e.g. `+10000000001:owner,+10000000002:support`). No real phones committed to git.

Run: `pnpm --filter @apps/api exec node --import tsx scripts/seed-platform-ops.ts`

### Team API

| Method | Path | Auth | Body |
|--------|------|------|------|
| `GET` | `/platform/v1/team` | read | — |
| `POST` | `/platform/v1/team` | **owner** | `{ "phone", "role": "owner" \| "admin" \| "support" }` |

Responses:

```json
{ "items": [{ "phone", "role", "createdAt" }] }
```

```json
{ "member": { "phone", "role", "createdAt" } }
```

Support role cannot POST team members (403).

### RBAC coverage

Every platform **mutator** (`POST`, `PATCH`, `DELETE` under `/platform/v1/*`) calls `assertPlatformOpsWriteRole` after auth. Team POST additionally requires `assertPlatformOpsOwnerRole`.

